## Dataset format

This dataset is distributed in [YOLO](https://docs.ultralytics.com/datasets/) training format:
image files split into `train`/`val`/`test` sets, described by a `data.yaml` config.

{% if class_names %}
It has {{ num_classes }} class{{ "es" if num_classes != 1 else "" }}: {{ class_names | join(", ") }}.
{% endif %}

```text
.
├── data.yaml             ← YOLO dataset config (splits, classes)
├── images/
│   ├── train/            ← training images
│   ├── val/               ← validation images
│   └── test/              ← test images (if present)
├── labels/                ← training labels (if present in the source dataset)
│   ├── train/
│   ├── val/
│   └── test/
├── checksums-sha256.txt
├── CITATION.cff
└── LICENSE
```
{% if sharded_splits %}

The {{ sharded_splits | join(", ") }} split{{ "s are" if sharded_splits | length > 1 else " is" }} too large
for a single Hugging Face Hub folder (10,000 files at most), so its images and labels are
spread over hash-named subfolders (e.g. `images/train/3f/img.jpg` with its label at
`labels/train/3f/img.txt`). YOLO trainers find them just the same: they look for images
recursively under each split's folder.
{% endif %}
